Feature: Presets
  The preset is how hot the kettle makes the water: WARM is 70 °C, HOT is 85 °C and BOIL is
  100 °C. PRESET steps through them, and back to WARM. The kettle starts on WARM. The child
  lock ignores it, like every other button.

  Expectation: WARM to HOT
    Given the preset is WARM
    And the child lock is off
    When the user presses preset
    Then the preset is HOT

  Expectation: HOT to BOIL
    Given the preset is HOT
    And the child lock is off
    When the user presses preset
    Then the preset is BOIL

  Expectation: BOIL back to WARM
    Given the preset is BOIL
    And the child lock is off
    When the user presses preset
    Then the preset is WARM
